he trick, "],["pg",""],["ls","sh"],["pc","hhh"],["pg",""],["hs","sh"],["at","South will have no way to return to his hand to enjoy his other 3 heart winners. "],["pg",""],["up","2"],["hs","sh"],["At","If instead South overtakes the @HJ with the @HK or @HQ, "],["pg",""],["ls","sh"],["pc","hqh"],["pg",""],["hs","shwd"],["at","West will discard on the third round of hearts "],["pg",""],["ls","shwd"],["pc","hkdsh"],["pg",""],["hs","ehsh"],["at","and East's control of the fourth round of that suit will leave South with no hope for the contract. "],["pg",""],["ls","ehsh"],["up","15"],["hs","nc"],["nt","South can, in fact, guarantee his contract by winning the first trick with dummy's @CA. "],["pg",""],["ls","nc"],["pc","cacc"],["pg",""],["hs","nh"],["at","South should continue by winning the next 2 tricks with dummy's @HA and @HJ, unblocking the suit. "],["pg",""],["ls","nh"],["pc","hahhh"],["pg",""],["pc","hhhh"],["pg",""],["hs","ncscwc"],["at","South has retained both the @CQ and @CJ in the closed hand and he can now force an entry to his long hearts by leading a club; it makes no difference whether the defenders win their @CK or hold up. "],["pg",""],["ls","wcncsc"],["pc","cccck"],["pg",""],["hs","wcsc"],["nt","West returns a club which South wins in hand. "],["pg",""],["ls","wcsc"],["pc","c9ccc"],["pg",""],["hs","sh"],["at","South is now able to cash 3 more heart winners "],["pg",""],["ls","sh"],["hs","nd"],["at","followed by 3 diamond tricks to emerge with an overtrick. "],["pg",""],["ls","nd"],["hs","wses"],["at","The defense could have prevented the overtrick by cashing 3 rounds of spades after winning the @CK, "],["pg",""],["ls","esws"],["hs","nc"],["up","19"],["at","but the contract was never in danger once South made the unusual (delayed) entry-preserving play of rising with the @CA at trick 1."],["",""]]}}